{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JdWScos5v6j7Pu3eAz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\nGood evening. My name is [NAME]. I've run a charter boat out of [HARBOR] for 22 years, one of 11 charter boats there.\n\nI'm not here to say the flounder don't need help. Your staff says the stock is at 78% of its target, and I believe them. Nobody needs those fish more than I do. I'm here to ask you to take the cut in a way that doesn't fall so hard on the boats that land the least.\n\nCharter boats land about 9% of this state's summer flounder. Private boats land about 80%. Most of the fish this cut saves will come from private boats. For us, the cut comes out of our livelihood.\n\nI can only speak for my own books, so here they are. When you cut the limit in 2016, my bookings fell from 170 trips to 138 the next season. That's 32 trips at $900 each, or $28,800 gone in one year. Two years later I was back up to 155, and I still hadn't reached where I started. That was one cut. This one runs three years.\n\nOur charter association asked 70 past customers what they would do if the limit drops to 2. Forty-one said they would book fewer trips. Twelve said they'd book the same. People don't pay $900 for a day on the water to bring home two fish.\n\nSo I'm asking you for a middle path. Set the limit at 3 fish, or keep 4 with a shorter season. Either one still protects the stock, and either one gives boats like mine a fighting chance to get through the next three years.\n\nThank you.\n</final_document>\n\nSome notes on the draft:\n\n- **Length:** about 290 words, which comes to roughly two minutes at a calm speaking pace. Read it aloud with a timer once. If you run long, cut the survey paragraph first.\n- **The \"every boat\" line:** I kept it out. You can't back it up, and you don't need it. \"I can only speak for my own books\" followed by your real 2016 numbers is harder to argue with than a prediction, and nothing in it can be challenged.\n- **\"Shorter season\":** I read this as keeping 4 fish with fewer open days. If you meant cutting to 2 fish but for fewer than 3 years, change the ask to \"or keep the cut to one year instead of three.\"\n- **The survey:** I gave your association's numbers as they are and made no claims about how customers were picked. If someone asks about the method, just say it was a survey of past customers and you don't have more detail."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1088,"cache_read_input_tokens":9841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1088},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81724ee3-0411-4577-a3be-f08db41b4ef3","uuid":"84de7b77-ae1c-4906-a550-449e1dc0ce60","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:19:20.779Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7JdWKSBuNzyowRxYGGm"}
